  "/destinations/south-dakota/rapid-city/tours/private-badlands-sunset-and-the-wonders-of-the-night-sky-457193": {
    "description": "Private Badlands Sunset And The Wonders of The Night Sky is a locally operated experience in Rapid City. Duration 8 Hours About Relax and enjoy a spectacular evening in the Badlands atop pinnacle overlook, as you witness the gorgeous Western South Dakota sun set over the peaks, valleys, and multicolored spires which make up the labyrinth of the wonderfully landscaped Badlands. The area, named Mako Sica by Indigenous people was formed over a period of 75 million years, and they are home to over 50 species of native grasses, Bison, Big Horned Sheep, Prairie Dogs, and other fauna. From there, take a short 30-minute drive to the small western town of Quinn, the home of The Badlands Observatory.",
    "headline": "8 hours",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/XznaFT8aRJeKhZPLdIsR"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "From there, take a short 30-minute drive to the small western town of Quinn, the home of The Badlands Observatory",
      "This astronomical observatory was founded in 2000 by Ron Dyvig and Theresa Hofer",
      "Ron has had a lifelong passion for astrology",
      "He designed and built many of the telescopes in the observatory and has identified more than 25 asteroids",
      "He assisted in the design and testing of the image intensifier camera systems"
    ]
  },
