  "/destinations/manawat-whanganui/taumarunui/tours/2-day-culturally-guided-paddle-taumarunui---whakahoro-480032": {
    "description": "2 Day Culturally Guided Paddle (Taumarunui - Whakahoro) is a locally operated experience in Taumarunui. Guests experience the Whanganui Awa with local Māori Kaitiaki on a fully guided, fully catered 2-day cultural river journey with free pre-trip accommodation. 2-Day Fully Guided & Catered Cultural Whanganui River Journey Experience the Whanganui Awa Through the Eyes of Tangata Whenua Discover the beauty, history and living culture of the Whanganui Awa on this unforgettable two-day guided river journey through the heart of Whanganui National Park. More than simply a canoe trip, this all-inclusive experience invites you to connect with one of New Zealand's most treasured landscapes alongside local Tangata Whenua Kaitiaki who were born and raised on the Whanganui River. The operator lists the duration as 2 days + 1 night.",
    "headline": "Experience the Whanganui Awa with local Māori Kaitiaki on a fully guided, fully catered 2-day cultural river journey with free pre-trip accommodation.",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/de60vng3TxGshhM01sTE",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/kHhOxZ41R0ScTbX3Z3qE",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/2c1emhxTSsygkYqWzpJa",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/lcNHgjqETuuZq5VSXyQN",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/6zeVm3U2S3a0eY4yjIpd",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/OyjpRT1KRtChidtkakmY",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/PtDkbfMQLqwzFkUni8Rg",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/gnZmFSuLRjmrrZMDfmh9"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "--- Start the guest's Adventure the Night Before the guest's experience begins before you even step onto the river",
      "Check-in is available :00 pm , with late arrivals welcome",
      "The operator's accommodation operates as a convenient self check-in facility",
      "The guest's room key will be waiting in the guest's allocated room",
      "The guest's Kaitiaki are more than guides—they are storytellers, guardians and descendants of the Whanganui Awa"
    ],
    "duration": "2 days + 1 night",
    "meetingPoint": "Complimentary accommodation at our Owhango Adventures base is available from **4:00 pm** on the afternoon prior to departure, with **late arrivals welcome**. Our accommodation operates as a **self check-in** facility, making your arrival simple and convenient. Upon arrival, enter through the guest entrance and check the **display board in the lounge area**, where you'll find your room allocation, departure time, guide information and any important updates relating to your journey. Your room key will be waiting in your allocated room. Staying with us the night before means you can relax, enjoy our shared guest facilities and wake refreshed for your adventure without the stress of an early morning drive. A cooked breakfast is served on the morning of departure before meeting your local Tangata Whenua Kaitiaki for a comprehensive safety briefing, paddling instruction and introduction to the journey ahead. All guests are required to complete a waiver form and attend the full safety briefing prior to departure. Following breakfast and trip preparation, you'll travel by shuttle to the **Nga Huinga** river launch site. Free secure vehicle parking is available at our Owhango Adventures base for the duration of your river journey."
  },
