  "/destinations/california/san-diego/tours/la-jolla-cove-2-tank-guided-shore-dives-107822": {
    "description": "La Jolla Cove 2-Tank Guided Shore Dives is a locally operated experience in San Diego. Age 13+ · Most Popular Tour · Certified Divers Only · Incl. dive-gear package. San Diego is a world-class scuba diving destination, and scuba divers from all over the world travel here to explore and photograph the numerous species of marine life found in the La Jolla Underwater Park. San Diego's most popular shore dive site is called La Jolla Cove. The operator lists the duration as Approximately 4 to 4.5 hours.",
    "headline": "Age 13+  ·  Most Popular Tour  ·  Certified Divers Only  ·  Incl. dive-gear package",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/i9solFWaT56xaP8iL7Iz",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/QuSjNTTUT6itCQxiFhEK",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/EGl37KKTsCFXFHN4nYzg",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/bItnBSfMSWyWpduoIWm9",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/QAkR52FiRPgpGvE6urDA",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/YMTiK1vsQHeqNE1jdaeC"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Includes Guaranteed small and personalized groups of 4 divers or fewer per instructor/dive guide A detailed site and marine biology briefing before every dive!",
      "Plan to bring Venmo, or just add to your credit/debit card on file.",
      "San Diego's most popular shore dive site is called La Jolla Cove",
      "The La Jolla Cove is located in beautiful La Jolla, adjacent to Scripps Park, which is inside an Ecological Reserve & Marine Sanctuary",
      "Within the Marine Reserve, it is unlawful to fish or remove anything (other than trash), which makes it great for observing marine life"
    ],
    "duration": "Approximately 4 to 4.5 hours",
    "meetingPoint": "- You have to be able to carry your own dive gear from the staging area, down the stairs to the beach. - This is not a physical building, but a park area at La Jolla Cove where you will meet your dive guide and group. More info is below. - All tours are SHORE DIVING (from the beach entry), NO BOAT DIVING into the La Jolla Marine Sanctuary (no boat). - If you opted to supply your own scuba gear setup, double-check and ensure its safe functioning and fully working condition. Your dive guide will not have any additional gear at the dive site, except for the usual dive tools, spares, and repair parts. If you experience any issues with your dive gear at the dive site, it will be too late to repair a regulator setup or BCDs or make any last-minute changes. - Your dive guide/instructor will bring steel tanks and soft-weight bags for your use during the dives. The weight amount will be according to your current weight and the use of a wet or dry suit. Please call us immediately if you need to make any changes to your current rental booking or if you need any additional rental gear before 3 pm tonight, so we can pack your gear accordingly. - There will be no refunds if the dives have to be canceled due to faulty gear at the dive site.",
    "included": [
      "Guaranteed small and personalized groups of 4 divers or fewer per instructor/dive guide A detailed site and marine biology briefing before every dive!"
    ],
    "notIncluded": [
      "Transportation from and to the dive site"
    ]
  },
