  "/destinations/vermont/essex-junction/tours/field-to-glass-a-meal-highlighting-vermonts-distilleries-425227": {
    "description": "Field to Glass: A Meal Highlighting Vermont's Distilleries is a locally operated experience in Essex Junction. Vermont Farm and Still Series Join us each month for an evening of pairing as we feature one of Vermont’s finest Spirits and source local ingredients from neighboring farms. Combining Vermont’s rich farming and distilling traditions with hands-on cooking is such a fun way to immerse everyone in the local flavors. The chance to learn from skilled chefs while crafting a four-course meal is a unique experience and finishing it off by sitting down together to enjoy the fruits of the guest's labor sounds like the perfect way to celebrate Vermont's culture.",
    "headline": "Field to Glass: A Meal Highlighting Vermont's Distilleries",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/N5ZCBxLRVuFwXGsh7LVJ"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Includes ##Menu may include:## -Bourbon Barrel Maple Brown Bread -Whistle Pig Rubbed Pork Belly -Sage Smashed Chicken with Vermont Silo Gin -Smuggler Notch Maple Cask Rum Cake",
      "Combining Vermont’s rich farming and distilling traditions with hands-on cooking is such a fun way to immerse everyone in the local flavors",
      "The operator's Chefs will instruct you step by step as they share their culinary knowledge and instruct proper cooking techniques",
      "Classes are hands-on, balancing passive and active tasks to create a four-course meal",
      "At the end of class, we all sit down to enjoy the meal together as we celebrate Vermont"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "#What to Expect - **Please plan to be in class 5 minutes before class begins so that we may take roll call.** If you have not yet paid for your class, please stop by the front desk on the way down to the kitchen. FOR HANDS ON CLASSES--- - **ATTIRE:**The Essex recommends that students wear closed-toe shoes to class and to dress appropriately for a cooking environment and have long hair tied back. Shorts, skirts, open-toed shoes, and flip flops are not allowed to be worn during any classes. The Essex will provide an apron to protect most clothing but, being a professional kitchen environment, spills do unfortunately happen. - **KITCHEN SAFETY:** Participants assume and accept that they will be participating in cooking activities where there is a natural element of risk of injury with kitchen appliances, equipment, knives, allergic reactions, and other participants in the class. When you reserve your cooking class you acknowledge this level of risk to yourself while participating in the activities at The Essex.",
    "included": [
      "##Menu may include:## -Bourbon Barrel Maple Brown Bread -Whistle Pig Rubbed Pork Belly -Sage Smashed Chicken with Vermont Silo Gin -Smuggler Notch Maple Cask Rum Cake"
    ]
  },
  "/destinations/vermont/essex-junction/tours/explore-vermont-maple-425233": {
    "description": "Explore Vermont Maple is a locally operated experience in Essex Junction. A meal celebrating Vermont's favorite flavor. Vermont Maple Cooking Class: Sweet & Savory Creations Join us for a hands-on cooking class dedicated to the finest Vermont maple syrup! In this class, guests can learn how to incorporate the natural sweetness of maple into both savory and sweet dishes that are perfect for any occasion. The operator lists the duration as 2.5 - 3 hours.",
    "headline": "A meal celebrating Vermont's favorite flavor",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/9XImV5ElSmyBoPttBMag"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Vermont Maple Cooking Class: Sweet & Savory Creations Join us for a hands-on cooking class dedicated to the finest Vermont maple syrup",
      "In this class, guests can learn how to incorporate the natural sweetness of maple into both savory and sweet dishes that are perfect for any occasion",
      "We’ll explore its versatility, pairing it with ingredients that highlight its rich, golden flavor"
    ],
    "duration": "2.5 - 3 hours"
  },
  "/destinations/vermont/essex-junction/tours/exploring-vermont-cheese-611245": {
    "description": "Exploring Vermont Cheese is a locally operated experience in Essex Junction. We explore Vermont's artisan cheeses and locally crafted beverages, creating an experience that celebrates Vermont’s rich agricultural heritage. This experience features a delightful Vermont Cheese Cooking Class, where guests can explore the art of creating small plates inspired by the state's renowned artisan cheeses. In this hands-on experience, guests can learn to prepare a variety of delectable dishes featuring Vermont's finest cheeses, from creamy chèvre to sharp cheddar and everything in between.",
    "headline": "Exploring Vermont Cheese",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/avAkz5CuTr2A9UfZ7VYG"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "We explore Vermont's artisan cheeses and locally crafted beverages, creating an experience that celebrates Vermont’s rich agricultural heritage",
      "Guests can discover the nuances of working with local cheeses, mastering techniques to enhance their unique flavors in each dish"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "#What to Expect - **Please plan to be in class 5 minutes before class begins so that we may take roll call.** FOR HANDS ON CLASSES--- - **ATTIRE:**The Essex recommends that students wear closed-toe shoes to class and to dress appropriately for a cooking environment and have long hair tied back. Shorts, skirts, open-toed shoes, and flip flops are not allowed to be worn during any classes. The Essex will provide an apron to protect most clothing but, being a professional kitchen environment, spills do unfortunately happen. - **KITCHEN SAFETY:** Participants assume and accept that they will be participating in cooking activities where there is a natural element of risk of injury with kitchen appliances, equipment, knives, allergic reactions, and other participants in the class. When you reserve your cooking class you acknowledge this level of risk to yourself while participating in the activities at The Essex. Bringing your own Alcoholic Beverages is strictly prohibited."
  },
  "/destinations/italy/linguaglossa/tours/etna-3000-and-2002-craters-615323": {
    "description": "Etna 3000 and 2002 Craters is a locally operated experience in Linguaglossa. 2 h and 30 minutes · Explore one of the most ancient lava flows and smoke-emitting craters. Etna 3000 starts from Piano Provenzana, one reaches an altitude of 2,900 meters by traveling with off-road vehicles along a high-mountain track, carved among suggestive expanses of lava and volcanic sand along the fracture that opened during the 2002 eruption. Continuing the operator's excursion with the operator's off-road vehicles up to an altitude of 2,840 meters, we reach the vulcanological observatory of Pizzi Deneri.",
    "headline": "2 h and 30 minutes  ·  Explore one of the most ancient lava flows and smoke-emitting craters",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/8ybRIHAYQg2jdeSutkMJ"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Includes Excursion and transport with 4X4 vehicles.",
      "Includes Volcanolgical guide for the duration of the excursion.",
      "From this point, the ascent on foot begins along a path surrounded by volcanic scoria and bombs",
      "The total ascent is 300 meters until reaching a panoramic point at an altitude of 2,900 meters",
      "With good weather, guests can see both the “Leone” valley and the “Bove” valley, as well as the majesty of the Northeast and Southeast craters"
    ],
    "included": [
      "Excursion and transport with 4X4 vehicles.",
      "Volcanolgical guide for the duration of the excursion."
    ]
  },
