  "/destinations/france/paris/tours/latin-quarter-walking-tour-443181": {
    "description": "Latin Quarter Walking Tour is a locally operated experience in Paris. In the tour the operator will see the oldest passage of Paris, where the oldest café of Paris is located (meeting point of philosophers and revolutionaries) the operator will see where the idea of the guillotine was created. An essential stop on this tour and undoubtedly one of the most impressive monuments in Paris is The Pantheon, conceived as a church dedicated to the patron saint of Paris Saint Genevieve will be converted in the resting place of great figures of the nation such as Victor Hugo, Voltaire, Rousseau, and Pierre and Marie Curie. On this 2 hours 15 minutes walk, the operator will be visiting La Sorbonne, the Luxembourg Gardens - the most beautiful and largest gardens in Paris, the oldest theatre of Paris: The Odeon, the operator will discover where Pablo Picasso painted one of the most important works of art of the 20th century, The Guernica, and a hidden work of art of Dali in one of the streets of the Latin Quarter.",
    "headline": "Latin Quarter Walking Tour",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/6KammXOLSW2wA7tswqbg"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Guests discover all that this Bohemian neighbourhood has to offer"
    ]
  },
