  "/destinations/florida/crystal-river/tours/crystal-river-clear-kayak-tour-manatee-season-tour-november---march-108118": {
    "description": "Crystal River Clear Kayak Tour | Manatee Season Tour (November - March) is a locally operated experience in Crystal River. A two-hour guided clear kayak tour through Kings Bay during manatee season, with a local guide who knows where to look! From mid-November through March, hundreds of manatees move into the warm spring-fed waters of Kings Bay — which is how Crystal River earned the name Manatee Capital of the World®. This is a two-hour guided paddle in a 100% clear tandem kayak.",
    "headline": "A two-hour guided clear kayak tour through Kings Bay during manatee season, with a local guide who knows where to look!",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/6qF50L1bTsGvqQ7RTOBX",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/UlwHktCnRWiWnpPLjJPc",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/EvryjZiSCwU4euwAMAFA",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/HuzOnMbUQ9CTkgNohIPO",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/0ayg30sSQ06vgz1PcBD9",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/rz8ba7gZQGC7NJKsfMda",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/tKBbnsMT0iLw2jYNBGoD",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/z1xFiPjzSqefk9ofn2dZ"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "This is a two-hour guided paddle in a 100% clear tandem kayak",
      "You stay in the boat the whole time, and when a manatee passes underneath, you watch the whole thing happen through the hull",
      "No wetsuit, no snorkel, and you go home dry",
      "The guest's guide is a local who's been reading these waters for years",
      "Where the manatees have been this week, where the water's clearest, which springs are worth the paddle that day"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Arrival Time: Please arrive 15 minutes early. Arriving more than 15 minutes late means missing the tour — we can't reschedule same-day. Parking: A parking fee is required by the city. Pay at the kiosk right at the parking lot entrance. Meeting Your Guide: Once parked, head down toward the water to our kayak corral — look for the A-frame sign. Your guide will check you in and run the safety briefing there. On the Water: Two hours of paddling with stops for photos. Your guide is happy to take them for you, so hand over your phone whenever you want. Dress Warm: Manatee season mornings on the water are colder than they look from the parking lot. Layers, and more than you think you need.",
    "notIncluded": [
      "Parking fee (required by city, payable by card upon arrival) Drinking Water"
    ]
  },
