  "/destinations/montana/livingston/tours/winter-wildlife-tours-653416": {
    "description": "Winter Wildlife Tours is a locally operated experience in Livingston. Ages 5+ · 1-3 day options · 6-8 hours per day. Winter is the best time to experience wildlife in Yellowstone, except for hibernating bears. With bears in their dens, bison, elk and moose stay lower and are more easily visible from the road. The operator lists the duration as 1-3 day options • 6-8 hours per day.",
    "headline": "Ages 5+  ·  1-3 day options  ·  6-8 hours per day",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/0DIH1DqQCaCtaHmvmHHg",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/N67mYmC1QpCP95NqYb11"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Winter is the best time to experience wildlife in Yellowstone, except for hibernating bears",
      "With bears in their dens, bison, elk and moose stay lower and are more easily visible from the road",
      "This also means wolves stay lower in the valleys, for a better chance of viewing",
      "Wolves have an easier time moving on top of snow, which allows them to hunt, explore and protect their territory from rival packs",
      "Snow brings out foxes, coyotes, otters, and other possible predators, too"
    ],
    "duration": "1-3 day options • 6-8 hours per day",
    "notIncluded": [
      "Cameras or lens, however I can give rental recommendations in Bozeman prior to tour"
    ]
  },
  "/destinations/montana/livingston/tours/winter-photography-tours-653419": {
    "description": "Winter Photography Tours is a locally operated experience in Livingston. Ages 5+ · 1-3 day options · 6-8 hours per day. Winter is the best time for wildlife photography in Yellowstone because wildlife sticks closer to the road. This is the best time to photograph the wolves of Yellowstone. The operator lists the duration as 1-3 day options • 6-8 hours per day.",
    "headline": "Ages 5+  ·  1-3 day options  ·  6-8 hours per day",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/fztkNxiwSMGkpYoJiXVN",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/PKUDekTfTGy8aeMmr9xe"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Winter is the best time for wildlife photography in Yellowstone because wildlife sticks closer to the road",
      "This is the best time to photograph the wolves of Yellowstone",
      "It is also the best time to photograph ungulates like moose, bison and elk, as well as foxes, coyotes, otters and the occasional owl",
      "Finding owls might require trekking in the backcountry which can be discussed prior to tour if interested",
      "Generally, each tour covers the northern range of Yellowstone, from Gardiner to Cooke City and back again"
    ],
    "duration": "1-3 day options • 6-8 hours per day",
    "notIncluded": [
      "Cameras or lens, however I can give rental recommendations in Bozeman prior to tour"
    ]
  },
