  "/destinations/united-states/hawaii/kihei/tours/5-hour-molokini-and-turtle-tour-551641": {
    "description": "5-Hour Molokini & Turtle Tour is a locally operated experience in Kihei. Guests experience sunrise at Molokini, snorkel two iconic Maui reefs, and enjoy a refreshing shoreside comfort stop on the operator's award-winning five-hour adventure. Be among the first boats to reach Molokini Crater at sunrise, snorkel its clear protected waters before the larger crowds arrive, and then continue to Maui’s famous Turtle Town in search of Hawaiian green sea turtles and vibrant marine life. Between snorkel destinations, enjoy a refreshing shoreside comfort stop with access to land-based restrooms, freshwater showers, fresh towels, and a chance to reset before the second half of the guest's adventure.",
    "headline": "Experience sunrise at Molokini, snorkel two iconic Maui reefs, and enjoy a refreshing shoreside comfort stop on our award-winning five-hour adventure.",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/HzgBrPg9S3yhyClu2hFw",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/OmnYVXjfRJ2BrwmrVMP6",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/mKkp5lvQzilyI0ndrLIu",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/l2LCzlX7QZa6RH0zFZHl",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/sUL6fDfsSK9s3v8d6t2E"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "The guest's adventure begins before the larger boats arrive, with a sunrise cruise toward Molokini Crater",
      "Watch the first light of the day rise over Haleakalā as Maui awakens around you",
      "Early mornings often provide lighter winds, calmer seas, cooler temperatures, clearer water, and fewer crowds—because the wind does not sleep in",
      "After snorkeling Molokini’s dramatic crater reef, we return briefly to shore for a comfortable mid-tour reset"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Please check in at 6:15 AM at Kihei Boat Ramp and look for the Maui Snorkel Charters crew at the Trailer parking. Look for the truck with the American Flag on the door. **Punctuality is essential. Guests must be checked in, waivers completed, equipment fitted, and ready to board before the scheduled departure.** Please allow additional time for: - Maui traffic - Parking - Restroom use - Locating the crew - Completing any outstanding waivers - Getting children and personal belongings organized Late arrivals may miss the vessel. Because the boat must depart on schedule, missed departures are considered no-shows and are not eligible for a refund, credit, reschedule, or tour extension."
  },
