  "/destinations/germany/mnchen/tours/mini-classic-bike-tour-incl-beer-garden-stop-4pm-188903": {
    "description": "Mini Classic Bike Tour incl. Beer Garden Stop @ 4pm is a locally operated experience in Mnchen. Likely to sell out! Book the guest's spot now! Running daily at 4 PM from mid-May to October, this is the guest's chance to cruise through the city's heart with the operator's world-famous Mike's Bike Tours flair. The guest's Adventure Highlights: Effortless City Exploration: Effortlessly glide through Munich's Old Town, uncovering iconic landmarks like the magnificent Odeonsplatz and a fascinating peek at various other highlights such as Odeonsplatz, the Residenz Courtyards, the Hofgarten, to name a few.",
    "headline": "Likely to sell out! Book your spot now!",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/92i5Uz7pRKWxjGym7tBn",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/dIssSP2HQgqKdwISZVzG",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/N3JwBS7eQJqZaeAhXCxk",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/kAmGtcY4QOi2bQTJOw3G",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/kkMcoQ9vSfeLwVtvTKUq",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/Zf7Ku5sTgOgVfffTLvH8",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/7gap25m2T9mXvgit1liY",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/95OcOjYOTpiddGrPR6BD"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "The Wild Side of Munich: Catch a glimpse of the famous (and infamous",
      ") English Garden nudist meadow and witness the daring river surfers taking on the Eisbach wave",
      "This isn't just a tour; it's a memory in the making",
      "Book the guest's spot now and experience the best of Munich on two wheels"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Thank you for booking the Mini Classic Tour! To ensure you have a safe and comfortable ride, here is some specific additional information, especially for your 4 PM start time. Check the Weather and Dress in Layers Munich weather can change quickly. A 4 PM tour means you'll be cycling through the late afternoon and into the early evening. Check the Forecast: Please check the local weather forecast for Munich on the day of your tour. Dress in Layers: This is the most important tip. It may feel warm at 4 PM, but temperatures can drop significantly as the sun sets. A light jacket or long-sleeved shirt that you can easily take off or put on is highly recommended. Rain Protection: Sudden rain showers are not uncommon. A lightweight, packable raincoat or rain jacket will be your best friend. We sell ponchos if you do not have any gear in our shop before th tour begins. Footwear: Wear comfortable, closed-toe shoes that are suitable for cycling. Avoid open-toed shoes or sandals. Important Reminders Arrive Early: Please arrive at our meeting point at Marienplatz 15 at least 5 minutes before your 4 PM start time. Listen to Your Guide: Your safety is our top priority. Please pay close attention to the safety briefing and your guide's instructions throughout the tour. Tour Duration: The tour will last approximately 150 minutes, so you should plan to be finished around 6:30 PM. This leaves you with a beautiful early evening to continue exploring Munich. Bring Cash to buy water etc. and to TIP your guide if he did a good job. It is always appreciated."
  },
