  "/destinations/texas/port-aransas/tours/louisiana-whooping-crane-reintroduction-progress-made-goals-still-to-be-achieved-with-sara-zimorski-louisiana-department-of-wildlife-and-fisheries-581906": {
    "description": "Louisiana Whooping Crane Reintroduction – Progress Made, Goals Still To Be Achieved with Sara Zimorski, Louisiana Department of Wildlife & Fisheries is a locally operated experience in Port Aransas. When you work with whooping cranes you have to be in it for the long haul, a commitment that often spans decades! Whooping cranes are a long-lived species, capable of living 20-30 years in the wild, but they are slow to reproduce, hence the need for patience and a long-term commitment. The Louisiana whooping crane reintroduction began 15 years ago and while much progress has been made there have also been challenges and the population is not yet self-sustainable. Meeting details: Note: This year, Whooping Crane Festival is going paperless! There will no tickets for this event. Please bring the ID of the ticket purchaser to the event so we can check your name off the manifest.",
    "headline": "Louisiana Whooping Crane Reintroduction – Progress Made, Goals Still To Be Achieved with Sara Zimorski, Louisiana Department of Wildlife & Fisheries",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/uNqsJVTR6HkxSM8Ca1Rw"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Includes Price includes admission to the event.",
      "When you work with whooping cranes you have to be in it for the long haul, a commitment that often spans decades"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Note: This year, Whooping Crane Festival is going paperless! There will no tickets for this event. Please bring the ID of the ticket purchaser to the event so we can check your name off the manifest.",
    "included": [
      "Price includes admission to the event."
    ]
  },
  "/destinations/texas/port-aransas/tours/community-connections-supporting-louisianas-whooping-crane-recovery-with-irvin-louque-and-brittney-palode-689746": {
    "description": "Community Connections: Supporting Louisiana’s Whooping Crane Recovery with Irvin Louque and Brittney Palode is a locally operated experience in Port Aransas. Community Connections: Supporting Louisiana’s Whooping Crane Recovery with Brittney Palode. Whooping Cranes are slowly returning to Louisiana's coastal and agricultural wetlands, but their recovery has been slowed by anthropogenic mortalities such as shootings. For four years, the International Crane Foundation (ICF) has been proactively engaging hunters, educating youth, and inspiring communities throughout the range of the Louisiana nonmigratory population of Whooping Cranes. Meeting details: Please arrive at least 15 minutes prior to start time. Refunds given only if Whooping Crane Festival cancels tour or event. Tickets will not be mailed to you. Tickets will be in your welcome packet.",
    "headline": "Community Connections: Supporting Louisiana’s Whooping Crane Recovery with Brittney Palode",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/AyMwyyzWRHyIav6zpTgf"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Since 2021, ICF has partnered with conservation organizations, state agencies, and libraries to introduce the Louisiana community to Whooping Cranes",
      "Their popular summer programs have reached hundreds of children each year in rural communities"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Please arrive at least 15 minutes prior to start time. Refunds given only if Whooping Crane Festival cancels tour or event. Tickets will not be mailed to you. Tickets will be in your welcome packet."
  },
