    "description": "Backcountry & Avalanche Mentorship is a locally operated experience in Cottonwood Heights. After years of teaching recreational avalanche courses and listening closely to feedback, we’ve taken the next step—reshaping how you learn about avalanches and backcountry travel on skis or a splitboard. This program combines the essential skills from Rescue, Rec Level 1, and Rec Level 2 into one comprehensive course. Running December through March, it’s designed so participants gain real experience in a variety of conditions and terrain, giving you the experience guests can need for a lifetime of safe backcountry travel. The operator lists the duration as This winter we have two 6-day sessions available—one on weekends and one on weekdays. Dates are provided below.",
