  "/destinations/maryland/denton/tours/public-maryland-style-fathers-day-june-15th-618960": {
    "description": "Public Maryland Style Father's Day June 15th is a locally operated experience in Denton. A Maryland Style Father's Day cruise for the guys! Celebrate Father's Day with a delicious Captain's Feast, featuring all things Maryland: crabs, shrimp, fried chicken, corn, watermelon, and more. The experience includes while sipping on beer from the operator's cash bar, all aboard a relaxing cruise on the Choptank River.",
    "headline": "A Maryland Style Father's Day cruise for the guys!",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/G0rPWVJPSaacUTfIJxtg"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Celebrate Father's Day with a delicious Captain's Feast, featuring all things Maryland: crabs, shrimp, fried chicken, corn, watermelon, and more",
      "The experience includes while sipping on beer from the operator's cash bar, all aboard a relaxing cruise on the Choptank River",
      "This experience features June 20th pm to 4pm for a memorable outing with that special guy in the guest's life",
      "The ticket price of includes refills of sweet tea, unsweet tea, lemonade, and water, the entire food spread, and the guest's boat fare",
      "The operator's river cruiser is Coast Guard Certified and is wheelchair accessible"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Please do not arrive more than 15 minutes prior to your cruise time, as we cannot accommodate you before this threshold. Do not exit your vehicle until boarding begins (10-15 minutes before the scheduled cruise time). We promise we will not leave without you - unless you're more than 5 minutes late with no attempts to contact us! Parking is in front of our office, 10282 River Landing Rd. Denton, MD 21629. Please DO NOT park in the Caroline County Yacht Club's parking lot. We want to be respectful neighbors! There are no bathrooms inside of our office. There are two portable restrooms located near our office building (one near the Yacht Club, one across the street from our office) that you are welcome and encouraged to use prior to boarding. One of our crew members will meet you at the end of our dock at boarding time and provide instructions."
  },
