  "/destinations/district-of-columbia/washington/tours/washington-dc-private-night-tour-four-hours-copy-683023": {
    "description": "Washington DC Private Night Tour • Four Hours (copy) is a locally operated experience in Washington. Guests experience the breathtaking beauty of the National Mall in Washington, D.C. on a private night tour. This Private Tour is perfect for folks who want to see the best of Washington DC and discover a new side of the city’s major memorials and monuments with just their friends and family! Meet the guest's guide, hop aboard the guest's vehicle, and set off with the guest's group.",
    "headline": "Experience the breathtaking beauty of the National Mall in Washington, D.C. on a private night tour.",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/wTXc4cJCQkShG2KFrVtq"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Plan to bring You're welcome to bring your own water bottle, but we'll provide one for you as well.",
      "Meet the guest's guide, hop aboard the guest's vehicle, and set off with the guest's group",
      "Guests can see highlights like the US Capitol, Washington Monument, Lincoln Memorial, MLK Memorial, Jefferson Memorial and more",
      "Guests can also have the opportunity to stop for photo breaks, all the while learning about the landmarks’ history from the guest's guide",
      "Tour times available: 9AM-1PM or 2PM-6PM Here is a list of some example memorials and landmarks we may stop to see on the tour"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "Experience a captivating three-hour private guided night tour, departing at 7:00 PM Independence Ave SW, Washington, DC (Department of Agriculture Jamie L. Whitten Building, conveniently located near the Smithsonian Metro Station). Our service includes round-trip transportation tailored for your group, with options accommodating 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, up to 10, 20, or 36 participants. You will be accompanied by an expert tour guide who will share rich history, engaging stories, and valuable insights at each landmark. The tour features over 16 stops, allowing ample time to savor the sights: - U.S. Capitol Building West Side (10–15 minutes) - Ulysses S. Grant Memorial (5 minutes) - The Peace Statue (5 minutes) - James Garfield Memorial (5 minutes) - Jefferson Memorial (15 minutes) - Martin Luther King Jr. Memorial (10 minutes) - Lincoln Memorial (15 minutes) - Korean War Memorial (10 minutes) - Vietnam War Memorial (15 minutes) - Iwo Jima Memorial (10 minutes) - World War II Memorial (10 minutes) - White House (10 minutes) - Eisenhower Memorial (10 minutes) - Washington Monument (10 minutes) - George Mason Memorial - FDR Memorial (15 minutes) - Albert Einstein Memorial (10 minutes) Additionally, the tour includes views of Ford’s Theater, the FBI Building, and the National Archives Building. Our comfortable buses and vans are equipped with phone chargers and umbrellas for your convenience. We look forward to providing you with an unforgettable experience."
  },
