    "meetingPoint": "- 10.00, rendezvous over Ireland’s finest freshly baked scones, tea & coffee at the House restaurant, 4 Main Street, Howth. - Assess the weather, tide & season and choose the best route for your unique day. - 10.30, walk up the village with a chance to grab last minute provisions and collect our trusty hound Loki, before we go off-road. - Explore the ever-changing habitats, woodlands, heathland & cliffs to Binn Éadair, HG Wells’ most beautiful view in the world. - Hike across the peninsula, around Shielmartin Hill to Sutton Martello Tower and Red-Rock, overlooking Dublin Bay and the Wicklow mountains. - Find the Howth Goats, highland cattle, giant pigs & marine life for a real safari. - Ascend the famous Howth cliff paths to the Baily Lighthouse and the Summit, enjoying awe-inspiring vistas. - Around 3pm, wrap it up at the Summit Inn for a well-deserved beverage and snack.",
