  "/destinations/florida/homestead/tours/journey-through-nine-mile-pond-nps-ranger-guided-canoe-adventure-648246": {
    "description": "Journey Through Nine Mile Pond: NPS Ranger-Guided Canoe Adventure is a locally operated experience in Homestead. On this 3 hour program at Nine Mile Pond, guests can be guided by park rangers through the sawgrass and mangroves. Guests can get opportunities to experience the Everglades wilderness and its diverse habitats, animals, human history, and the vital water of the “river of grass”. This trip can be very strenuous!",
    "headline": "Journey Through Nine Mile Pond: NPS Ranger-Guided Canoe Adventure",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/XSSKY4YERRGnPCmKwrDO"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "On this 3 hour program at Nine Mile Pond, guests can be guided by park rangers through the sawgrass and mangroves",
      "This trip can be very strenuous",
      "Please consider the guest's abilities and only sign up if you are physically fit and have prior canoeing experience"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "You will check-in with a park ranger at Nine Mile Pond, about 25 miles past the Ernest F. Coe Visitor Center. Allow up to 45 minutes for this drive. Follow signs for Nine Mile Pond. Please arrive at least 30 minutes early to check-in (arrive by 8 am). If you are late, we reserve the right to give another visitor your place. Adults over the age of 18 must complete and submit their own waiver. Minors ages 17 and younger must have a parent or legal guardian sign a waiver on behalf of the minor. All minors must have an adult in the canoe with them."
  },
  "/destinations/florida/homestead/tours/paddling-in-paradise-ranger-guided-kayaking-on-florida-bay-648259": {
    "description": "Paddling in Paradise: Ranger-Guided Kayaking on Florida Bay is a locally operated experience in Homestead. On this three-hour program on Florida Bay, guests can be guided by park rangers through the mangrove estuaries and marine ecosystem. Guests can get opportunities to experience the Everglades wilderness and its diverse habitats, animals, and human history. This trip can be extremely strenuous!",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/jOIhxN1fQkWanbtbwVNf",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/xQBF84ASHGbwjVRCudRA",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/uxYWDQvKR26uRcJhwGuQ"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "On this three-hour program on Florida Bay, guests can be guided by park rangers through the mangrove estuaries and marine ecosystem",
      "Guests can get opportunities to experience the Everglades wilderness and its diverse habitats, animals, and human history",
      "This trip can be extremely strenuous",
      "Therefore, all participants are required to be at least 16 years old",
      "Please consider the guest's abilities and only sign up if you are physically fit and have prior kayaking experience"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "You will check-in with a park ranger at the Florida Bay Marina, about 40 miles past the Ernest F. Coe Visitor Center. Allow up to 60 minutes for this drive. Follow signs for Flamingo. Please arrive at least 30 minutes early to check-in (arrive by 8 am). If you are late, we reserve the right to give another visitor your place. Upon arrival, you will be required to sign a waiver before joining the tour. Adults over the age of 18 must complete and submit their own waiver. Minors ages 17 and younger must have a parent or legal guardian sign a waiver on behalf of the minor. All minors must have an adult in the kayak with them."
  },
