  "/destinations/florida/marco-island/tours/keewaydin-shelling-tour-442030": {
    "description": "Keewaydin Shelling Tour is a locally operated experience in Marco Island. Escape to Keewaydin Island on a 6-hour shelling trip from Marco Island. Guided by local naturalists, explore uncrowded beaches & protected waters. 6-Hour Keewaydin Island Shelling & Eco Tour Step into a true island escape on our 6-Hour Keewaydin Island Shelling & Eco Tour , where guests can enjoy unhurried time on one of Southwest Florida’s most beautiful boat-access-only barrier islands. Small-Group Shared Experience: Capped at a maximum of 6 guests per boat, this shared excursion provides a relaxed, uncrowded adventure with plenty of space to explore at the guest's own pace. The operator lists the duration as This activity lasts for approximately six hours.",
    "headline": "Escape to Keewaydin Island on a 6-hour shelling trip from Marco Island. Guided by local naturalists, explore uncrowded beaches & protected waters.",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/RlDWascT2aX8IYkNvHA3",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/GzW575pESYqVjn5lsNcf",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/J6z9MnOOS06YCKRyVccB",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/oXlrk1CLRM6SUcdMhcTX",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/IBAGNX4QxOq0RItpfMdY",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/qEOUojXYS9KbESZhYFqx",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/Nomfa9ixTTylj0zQ4Uov",
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/QXCGolfWTuehjhtplls5"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "100% Eco-Friendly Shelling: Sustainable, ethical practices are followed at every stop",
      "We strictly collect empty shells only to preserve the delicate coastal environment and living marine habitats",
      "A Keewaydin tour is the guest's day to explore, reconnect, and treasure the coast"
    ],
    "duration": "This activity lasts for approximately six hours.",
    "meetingPoint": "### Check-In & Departure Details * **Departure Location:** Goodland Boat Park 750 Palm Point Dr., Goodland, FL 34140 *(Just minutes from Marco Island)* * **Arrival Time:** Please arrive 15–20 minutes prior to your scheduled departure time to allow time for parking, using shore restrooms, and boarding. * **Meeting Location:** Meet your captain directly by the flagpole near the main boat launch area at Goodland Boat Park. * **Parking & County Fees:** * ** daily parking fee** enforced by Collier County, payable by credit card only at the automated park kiosk. * Parking is **free** for vehicles displaying a valid Collier County Resident Beach Parking Permit. * Overflow parking is available along the fence line outside the main gates if the primary lot is full. * **Footwear Requirement:** Closed-toe water shoes or neoprene booties are required for boarding and walking on shell beaches. Flip-flops and sandals are not permitted for safety reasons."
  },
