  "/destinations/new-york/brooklyn/tours/brooklyn-navy-yard-bicycle-tour-19349": {
    "description": "Brooklyn Navy Yard Bicycle Tour is a locally operated experience in Brooklyn. About Hop on the guest's bike and explore what was once America's premier Naval shipyard, and is today a mission-driven industrial park and a hub of industry, technology, and craft. On these guided explorations of this 300-acre site, visitors will get to see up close the many layers of history visible in the landscape, from Civil War-era machine shops to innovative LEED-Certified structures, and see how these buildings have been adapted for modern manufacturing. The operator's Past, Present & Future Bicycle Tour is a great introduction to the Yard, with a bit of history and a bit of the modern day to give a rounded picture of the whole site.",
    "headline": "Brooklyn Navy Yard Bicycle Tour",
    "images": [
      "http://turnstiletours.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/Brooklyn_Navy_Yard_Directions.jpeg"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "In addition to the Yard's long naval history, riders will also learn about projects currently underway at the Yard",
      "The tour covers most of the massive 300-acre campus, including visits to the still-active 1851 Dry Dock No",
      "1, the one-million-square-foot World War II-era Building 77, and the sites of the Admirals Row and Dock 72 projects",
      "Other veterans and military personnel are eligible for a 25% discount",
      "Call (347) 903-8687 or visit the operator's contact page for details"
    ]
  },
  "/destinations/new-york/brooklyn/tours/brooklyn-navy-yard-urban-ecology-bicycle-tour-19351": {
    "description": "Brooklyn Navy Yard: Urban Ecology Bicycle Tour is a locally operated experience in Brooklyn. Bicycle (not provided) · Select Sundays, 10:30am. About Discover the natural world in the midst a thriving urban industrial park on this 2-hour tour of the Brooklyn Navy Yard, where the operator will explore New York City’s waterways, terrestrial ecosystems and urban farms. At the stunning 65,000-square-foot Brooklyn Grange rooftop farm, the operator will learn how they produce thousands of pounds of vegetables annually – as well as honey and eggs – and are a national leader in the development of rooftop and urban farming techniques.",
    "headline": "Bicycle (not provided)  ·  Select Sundays, 10:30am",
    "images": [
      "http://turnstiletours.com/wp-content/uploads/2013/06/Brooklyn_Navy_Yard_Directions.jpeg"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "This tour will reveal that the natural world truly is all around us, even in the heart of the city",
      "Visit the operator's website for information on nearby bicycle rental shops",
      "- Dress appropriately for the weather and wear comfortable shoes",
      "- the operator will cycle approximately 5 miles on this tour",
      "- Cancellations: We cannot reschedule or refund tickets that are canceled within 24 hours of the tour start time"
    ]
  },
