  "/destinations/minnesota/duluth/tours/cat-lounge-visit-age-requirement-12-539963": {
    "description": "Cat Lounge Visit (Age Requirement: 12+) is a locally operated experience in Duluth. Ages 12+ · 50 Minutes. Come for the coffee, stay for the cats 50 Minute Session | Ages 12+ - Teen Admissions (Age 12-16): Must be supervised by an adult 18+ at all times about Book a 50-minute session at Wired Whisker's cat lounge, where guests can interact with adoptable rescue cats in a serene and joyful environment. Perfect for families, friends, or anyone looking to enjoy some quality time with the operator's playful feline residents.",
    "headline": "Ages 12+  ·  50 Minutes",
    "images": [
      "https://cdn.filestackcontent.com/NmcSumNRR0GhDObXOZNU"
    ],
    "highlights": [
      "Includes Enjoy time in our cat lounge",
      "Includes a relaxing space filled with adorable and adoptable rescue cats!",
      "Perfect for families, friends, or anyone looking to enjoy some quality time with the operator's playful feline residents",
      "More info - Visits to the cat lounge start on the hour, and are 50 minutes",
      "- Please note, these sessions are for ages 12+"
    ],
    "meetingPoint": "#cat lounge terms - Always check-in at the cafe counter before entering the lounge. - Upon entry, and leaving, make sure the first door is closed before opening the second so cats do not escape. - Use hand sanitizer before entering and exiting the cat lounge. - Do NOT wake a sleeping cat. (Soft pets and photos, no flash, are fine) - Do NOT pick up cats. (Unless they sneak into the double doorway. In that case only you can help them safely back into the cat lounge.) - Do NOT use your fingers or toes to play with cats, pull on, push, or chase a cat. - No treats from home or other establishments allowed. Do NOT feed cats any human food or drinks. Make sure to watch any food/beverage you bring into the room and take it out with you as well. #what not to bring - Outside Food or Drinks: To ensure the health and safety of our cats, outside food and beverages are not permitted. Our cafe offers a variety of delicious options for you to enjoy. - Large Bags or Backpacks: For the comfort and safety of our cats, we ask that you leave large bags or backpacks at home or store them in designated areas upon arrival. - Pets: As much as we love all animals, for the safety and comfort of our resident cats, other pets are not allowed within the cafe or lounge. #extra reminders (kids) - Do NOT touch the cat food or water! - Do NOT climb on the furniture. Furniture is for butts, NOT feet. - Use inside voices. (No screaming.) - No running please. (This can scare the cats.) important - Cats can bite and scratch. Use common sense around the cats. - You are welcome to leave coats and large bags in the double doorway upon entry. - Leave your cat (and all pets) at home. They will not be allowed in the cat lounge or cafe. - We do not guarantee that any cat will still be available for adoption at your visit or be at the cafe. - Respect the Cats' Space: If a cat walks away or seems uninterested in interaction, respect its space and do not force attention on it. - Report Concerns: If you notice anything that concerns you about a cat's well-being or behavior, report it to the staff immediately. - Follow Staff Instructions: Always follow any additional instructions or guidelines provided by the cafe staff and volunteers. They are there to ensure a safe and enjoyable experience for both the cats and visitors. - Anyone not adhering to the rules will be asked to leave and no refund given. By adhering to these rules, visitors can help ensure a pleasant and safe environment for everyone involved.",
    "included": [
      "Enjoy time in our cat lounge",
      "a relaxing space filled with adorable and adoptable rescue cats!"
    ],
    "notIncluded": [
      "Food and drinks"
    ]
  },
